rs/jasonyb/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false}],"milestone":null,"comments":0,"created_at":"2025-07-17T23:45:11Z","updated_at":"2025-08-06T18:38:27Z","closed_at":"2025-08-06T18:38:27Z","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"Jira Link: [DB-17629](https://yugabyte.atlassian.net/browse/DB-17629)\r\n### Description\n\nUsing session parameter (GUC) `yb_debug_log_docdb_requests=on`, one can see the number of read flushes does not match `EXPLAIN (ANALYZE, DIST)`'s `Catalog Read Requests`.  This is due to catalog prefetching/preloading at connection startup getting counted.\n\n```\nbin/yb-ctl start --ysql_pg_conf_csv yb_debug_log_docdb_requests=on --tserver_flags vmodule=pg_session=2 && sleep 3 && bin/ysqlsh\n```\n\n```sql\ncreate table rrr (r1 int, r2 int, r3 int, n int, primary key (r1 asc, r2, r3)) split at values ((0, 1), (1), (1, 1), (2), (2, 1));\n```\n\nexit ysqlsh, then reconnect (for fresh cache), then run:\n\n```sql\nexplain (analyze, dist, debug) select * from rrr where r1 in (0, 1, 2) order by r2 limit 2;\n```\n\nIt gives `Catalog Read Requests: 73` and `Metric ql_read_latency: sum: 1194, count: 8`.  Logs show 76 `vlog2: Apply`, 6 of which are for the table, 1 catalog lookup which is after EXPLAIN ANALYZE.  So it should say 69 catalog read requests.\n\n### Issue Type\n\nkind/bug\n\n### Warning: Please confirm that this issue does not contain any sensitive information\n\n- [x] I confirm this issue does not contain any sensitive information.\n\n[DB-17629]: https://yugabyte.atlassian.net/browse/DB-17629?atlOrigin=eyJpIjoiNWRkNTljNzYxNjVmNDY3MDlhMDU5Y2ZhYzA5YTRkZjUiLCJwIjoiZ2l0aHViLWNvbS1KU1cifQ","closed_by":{"login":"yugabyte-ci","id":17281578,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3MjgxNTc4","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercon